      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a report for a luxury lifestyle brand and we need to categorize some of the current trends and slang circulating on tiktok and reels. we want to see what's \"high-end/aspirational\" vs what's \"street-level/mass-market\" so we know what to avoid. \n\ncan you help me group these into 'sophisticated/premium' and 'vernacular/niche' categories?\n\ntrends/slang:\n1. drill music lyrics/slang (e.g. 'opps', 'glizzy')\n2. cottagecore aesthetic\n3. reggaeton/bad bunny style vibes\n4. minimal/quiet luxury aesthetic\n5. 'slaying' / 'periodt'\n6. indie sleaze revival\n7. trap music subculture\n8. old money aesthetic\n\ncan you break these down by their perceived social sophistication and who the primary audience seems to be?",
